{"name":"Pelagic","hex":"#355d83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pelagic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Living in the open sea rather than in coastal or inland waters.","Of or pertaining to oceans."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any organism that lives in the open sea rather than in coastal or inland waters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pelagic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pelagic zone","blocks":[{"text":"The pelagic zone consists of the water column of the open ocean and can be further divided into regions by depth. The word pelagic is derived from Ancient Greek  πέλαγος (pélagos) 'open sea'. The pelagic zone can be thought of as an imaginary cylinder or water column between the surface of the sea and the bottom."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelagic_zone","wikidata":"Q191468"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Representative_ocean_animal_life.jpg/500px-Representative_ocean_animal_life.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Representative_ocean_animal_life.jpg/500px-Representative_ocean_animal_life.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Some representative ocean animals (not drawn to scale) within their approximate depth-defined ecological habitats. Marine microorganisms also exist on the surfaces and within the tissues and organs of the diverse life inhabiting the ocean, across all ocean habitats. The animals rooted to or living on the ocean floor are not pelagic but are benthic animals.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARepresentative_ocean_animal_life.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hydrophis_platurus_118933110.jpg/500px-Hydrophis_platurus_118933110.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.w